# Living Uganda — copyright and reuse

Copyright © 2026 Living Uganda. All rights reserved except as set out below.

Living Uganda is an independent, non-commercial project documenting Uganda's
living world. The text, the site design, the original data compilations and the
code in this repository are the work of the project.

## What you may do without asking

- Read, link to and cite the site.
- Quote short passages with attribution ("Living Uganda, <page>, accessed <date>").
- Use it in teaching, study and non-commercial research.
- Print pages for personal or classroom use.

## What needs permission

- Reproducing substantial parts of the site or the catalogue in another
  publication, dataset or product.
- Commercial use of any kind.
- Re-hosting the site or its data under another name.

Please ask first: https://github.com/arsenebaguma0-ux/living-uganda/issues

## Third-party material keeps its own licence

This notice covers only material that Living Uganda itself created.

- **Photographs and illustrations** remain the property of their photographers
  and are used under the licence named beside each image on
  `credits.html`, `catalogue-credits.html` and `collection-credits.html`.
  Those licences (for example CC BY, CC BY-SA, CC0) control reuse of the images,
  not this notice.
- **Datasets** come from GBIF publishers under their own licences, listed on
  `dataset-credits.html`.
- **Typefaces** are Chakra Petch and IBM Plex Mono, used under the SIL Open Font
  License; the licence texts are in `assets/fonts/`.
- **Scientific sources** quoted or summarised on the site remain under the
  copyright of their authors and publishers.

If you believe something here is credited wrongly or used without permission,
please open an issue and it will be reviewed promptly.

## No warranty

The catalogue is a preliminary, growing record assembled from published
datasets. It is provided as-is, without warranty of accuracy or completeness,
and it is not a substitute for a formal taxonomic or conservation assessment.
